theory.intro:
Each straight segment of a distance–time graph is travelled at a constant speed, and the size of its steepness gives the speed. Read the distance covered (the **rise**) and the time taken (the **run**), then divide. On the same axes, steeper means faster; a horizontal segment gives speed $0$.

